<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kourou</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kourou is a town on the coast of French Guiana, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cayenne">Cayenne</a>. It was the scene of the disastrous <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kourou-expedition">Kourou expedition</a> of 1763, in which most of the thousands of French and German settlers died of disease. Since the 1960s it has grown around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guiana-space-centre">Guiana Space Centre</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s main spaceport, which made its first launch in 1968.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kourou.jpg" alt="Kourou" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: mike from New York, NY, US · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Centre_Spatial_Guyanais_(46886212831).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
